Let’s break it down further (as humans are wont to do). The right hand and left brain are linked through neurological connections. The left brain is known to science as the center of logic and analysis. Since most people are using their right hand to manipulate the world around them, they tend to think more analytically. This is the basis of CIII. If the right hand is the manipulator and the left brain the map maker, that means the artifacts the manipulator makes become the symbol systems used to make maps. Language:artifacts (both written and spoken) are solidified through internal logic, and an understanding of the world:model is made in a simplified shorthand that’s easy to pick up and put down as needed.

